 "text": "Hello there! How's life treating you? On the back of a driveway, or standing up at the end of it if it' long. Or near a tree if it's small one. That's a great spot. Tent poles keep it up and you' barely notice it. You can cut it off at the tent and redo the whole branch once home. Or leave it and use it for something like a torch stick. Keep it away from the smoke and direct wind gusts. In front of the tent is usually the nicest view, so you want full access there. That's it. Put a groundsheet down once the tent is up and you'll barely notice it.",
